      "body": "## Motivation\n\nTwo GSM8K thresholds in `test_quark_mxfp4.py` sit inside the normal run-to-run spread of the scores they check, so `stage-b-test-1-gpu-small-amd-mi35x` fails on them regularly with no code change. #41793 has failed on this file four times in a row and never reached its own test:\n\n| Attempt | Failing test | Scores (try, retry) | Threshold |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [2](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36653184760/attempts/2) | `TestFP8ToMXFP4MOETP1` | 0.904, 0.910 | 0.92 |\n| [3](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36653184760/attempts/3) | `TestFP8ToMXFP4MOETP1` | 0.912, 0.918 | 0.92 |\n| [4](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36653184760/job/110158770073) | `TestFP8ToMXFP4MOETP1` | 0.912, 0.912 | 0.92 |\n| [5](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36653184760/job/110210253573) | `TestNVFP4ToMXFP4MOETP1` | 0.810, 0.822 | 0.85 |\n\nThese are not regressions. The PR runs used the same code as a scheduled `main` run that passed. The scores come from the September 2026 PR Test (AMD) scheduled and dispatched runs of this lane, across the rocm700/10/720/724 images. All four images show the same distribution.\n\n| Test | Samples | Mean | Std | Min | Max | First try at or below threshold | Both tries at or below threshold |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `TestFP8ToMXFP4MOETP1` (0.92) | 101 | 0.924 | 0.009 | 0.900 | 0.946 | 30% | 13% of runs |\n| `TestNVFP4ToMXFP4MOETP1` (0.85) | 55 | 0.856 | 0.018 | 0.802 | 0.886 | 31% | 18% of runs |\n\nThe retry re-scores on the same server, so it rarely rescues a low first try. Together the two tests fail the lane in about 30% of runs. Because the suite stops at the first failure, every file after this one (19 of 49) is skipped too.\n\nNotes on the original comments:\n- The `~0.948` on `TestFP8ToMXFP4MOETP1` is the FP8 checkpoint's own score. Requantizing to MXFP4 costs about 2.5 points, so 0.92 was within one standard deviation of the requantized mean when it was added.\n- The `~0.88` on `TestNVFP4ToMXFP4MOETP1` is above what CI measures.\n\n## Modifications\n\n| Test | Threshold before | Threshold after | Distance below mean |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `TestFP8ToMXFP4MOETP1` | 0.92 | 0.89 | 3.8 standard deviations |\n| `TestNVFP4ToMXFP4MOETP1` | 0.85 | 0.79 | 3.7 standard deviations |\n\nBoth new thresholds are below every score observed in September, and the comments now record the observed spread. A real requantization bug still trips them. A broken MXFP4 MoE path lands far below either value, not a few points lower.\n\nNothing else in the file changes. The other thresholds already have enough margin; for example, the Dense TP1/TP2 tests check 0.868 against observed scores of 0.88-0.908.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] CI: `stage-b-test-1-gpu-small-amd-mi35x (rocm10)` passes `test_quark_mxfp4.py`\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #36866676516](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36866676516)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #36866693536](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36866693536)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #36866676354](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36866676354)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
